      { q: "Do I need HOA approval for a deck in Herndon VA?", a: "It depends on your neighborhood. Worldgate, Fox Mill Estates, and newer Silver Line-area communities have active HOAs with design review requirements. Older in-town Herndon neighborhoods near downtown are more varied — some have HOAs, some do not. Verify your property's HOA status before starting any design work. For properties with HOAs, approval must be obtained before the building permit is applied for." },
      { q: "How much does a deck cost in Herndon VA?", a: "Composite deck costs in Herndon in 2026 range from $27,000 to $43,000 for a 300-square-foot replacement and $30,000 to $47,000 for a new addition. Multi-level decks run $52,000 to $82,000. Screened porch additions run $36,000 to $65,000. Herndon pricing is consistent with the broader Northern Virginia market for comparable specifications." },
      { q: "Are there special requirements for decks near Herndon's Silver Line corridor?", a: "Newer residential developments near the Herndon and Innovation Center Silver Line stations tend to have well-documented HOA design standards with explicit material and color requirements. These are typically more detailed than older community guidelines. Some properties near the transit corridor may also be subject to specific zoning overlay requirements — verify with the Town of Herndon or Fairfax County planning staff based on your jurisdiction." },
      { q: "How long does a Herndon deck permit take?", a: "Town of Herndon building permit review for a standard deck typically takes 3 to 6 weeks. Fairfax County permit review (for properties outside town limits) takes 4 to 8 weeks. HOA approval adds 3 to 6 weeks concurrently. LDN Decks submits HOA and permit applications simultaneously at contract signing to minimize total elapsed time." }
