      { q: "Does South Riding HOA approve composite decking?", a: "Yes. The South Riding Proprietary accepts composite decking from major brands (Trex, TimberTech, AZEK) in natural wood-tone color families consistent with the home's exterior and community character. Submissions require a complete ARC application with site plan, elevation drawings, material specifications with manufacturer color references, and photographs. The Proprietary review takes 30 days for complete submissions. LDN Decks prepares complete South Riding Proprietary submissions for every project." },
      { q: "Does South Riding have village sub-associations in addition to the main HOA?", a: "Yes. South Riding is divided into villages, some of which have their own sub-association in addition to the master South Riding Proprietary. In some cases, village-level approval is required in addition to Proprietary approval, creating a two-step HOA process. LDN Decks confirms the applicable approval chain — Proprietary only, or Proprietary plus village association — at project outset for every South Riding project." },
      { q: "How much does a deck cost in South Riding VA?", a: "Composite deck replacement in South Riding runs $27,000 to $43,000 for 300 square feet. New composite additions run $29,000 to $46,000. Townhouse deck additions run $11,000 to $20,000. Multi-level decks run $50,000 to $80,000. South Riding pricing is consistent with the eastern Loudoun County market for comparable specifications." },
      { q: "What age are South Riding VA decks and do they need replacement?", a: "South Riding homes were built primarily from 1995 to 2005, making original pressure-treated wood decks now 20 to 30 years old. This is the primary replacement age range — surface deterioration (splintering, checking, gray weathering) is visible, railing connections may have loosened, and some early structural issues are appearing at ledger connections and post bases. South Riding's replacement market is active precisely because this housing stock is at the right age for composite upgrades." }
