      { q: "How much does a deck cost in Aldie VA?", a: "Composite deck replacement in Stone Ridge and standard Aldie communities runs $28,000 to $44,000 for 300 square feet. Willowsford premium-spec projects run $31,000 to $50,000. New composite additions run $29,000 to $47,000. Multi-level decks run $52,000 to $83,000. Willowsford carries premium ranges because homeowners select higher-specification natural-appearance products to match the community's character." },
      { q: "Does Willowsford HOA review railing design for decks?", a: "Yes. Willowsford's architectural standards address railing style and design as well as decking material. Railing must be compatible with the home's architectural style — craftsman and farmhouse-inspired railing designs are preferred. Traditional baluster railings in compatible colors are consistently accepted. Cable railing may be acceptable depending on the specific home and its architectural context, but requires careful ARC presentation." }
