    sourceLinks: COMPOSITE_BRAND_SOURCE_LINKS,
    excerpt: "Hamilton is a small historic town in western Loudoun County along Route 7, situated between Purcellville and Leesburg. Unlike eastern Loudoun's large planned communities, Hamilton and the surrounding rural corridor is characterized by older home stock, larger lot sizes, and the absence of HOA governance on most properties — creating a distinct deck project environment from the typical Loudoun County suburban community.",
    content: "Hamilton is a small historic town in western Loudoun County, situated along Route 7 between Purcellville and Leesburg. Unlike most of eastern Loudoun's large planned communities, Hamilton and its surrounding rural area is characterized by older home stock, larger lot sizes, and the absence of HOA governance on most properties — creating a distinct deck project environment from the typical Loudoun County suburban community.\n\n## Permit Authority: Loudoun County\n\nHamilton is an incorporated town in Loudoun County. Structural deck permits are issued by the Loudoun County Department of Building and Development:\n\n- Building permit required for decks 30 inches or more above grade or greater than 200 square feet\n- Site plan showing lot, existing structures, proposed deck, and all setbacks\n- Structural drawings: footing (21-inch frost depth), framing plan, ledger attachment, railing specifications\n- Plan review: 4 to 8 weeks for standard residential decks\n- No HOA required on most Hamilton properties — owner approval only, no ARB submission\n\n## Western Loudoun Deck Character\n\nHamilton and the surrounding rural western Loudoun corridor has a distinct deck project character from eastern Loudoun's planned communities:\n\n**Older home stock:** Many Hamilton-area homes date from the 1960s through 1990s — significantly older than Ashburn, Brambleton, or South Riding. Older homes require more thorough ledger and rim joist evaluation before deck work begins. LDN Decks reviews structural conditions at the home during the estimate process on all western Loudoun projects.\n\n**Larger lot sizes:** Hamilton properties tend toward half-acre to multi-acre lots. Larger lots allow more flexibility in deck design — setback constraints are less limiting than in high-density Loudoun subdivisions, and deck footprints can be designed based on the homeowner's outdoor living vision rather than lot coverage constraints. Wraparound decks, multi-wing designs, and large multi-level configurations are more feasible on western Loudoun lots.\n\n**No HOA on most properties:** The absence of HOA architectural review means the permit process is simpler — no ARB submission, no review wait period, no color or material approval required beyond Loudoun County's structural review. This compresses the timeline from contract to construction start compared to planned communities.\n\n**Material preferences:** Western Loudoun homeowners working on older properties often prefer natural materials — western red cedar, ipe hardwood, and higher-tier pressure-treated products are more commonly requested in western Loudoun than in eastern Loudoun planned communities where composite dominates. LDN Decks builds in all these materials and can advise on the right material for each property and use case.\n\n## Hamilton VA Deck Costs 2026\n\n- **Composite deck replacement (300 sq ft):** $25,000 to $40,000\n- **Western red cedar deck (300 sq ft):** $22,000 to $35,000\n- **Ipe hardwood deck (300 sq ft):** $30,000 to $50,000\n- **Large custom deck (500+ sq ft, larger rural lot):** $50,000 to $90,000\n- **Older home structural remediation (ledger or rim joist):** add $2,000 to $7,000 as needed\n\n[Contact LDN Decks for a Hamilton VA Deck Estimate](/get-estimate)\n\n---\n\n**Related:** [Deck Builder Purcellville VA](/blog/deck-builder-purcellville-va) · [Deck Builder Leesburg VA](/blog/deck-builder-leesburg-va) · [Composite vs Wood Decking Virginia](/composite-deck-vs-wood-deck-virginia) · [Deck Cost Northern Virginia 2026](/blog/how-much-does-deck-cost-northern-virginia-2026) · [New Deck Services](/services/new-decks)",
