      { q: "Do I need HOA approval for a deck in Hamilton VA?", a: "Most Hamilton VA properties do not have HOA governance — they are individual lots or rural properties outside any planned community. For these properties, deck work requires only a Loudoun County building permit and homeowner approval. No ARB submission, no material approval, and no color review are required. Some Hamilton-area subdivisions may have HOA covenants; verify your deed restrictions before starting any project." },
      { q: "How much does a deck cost in Hamilton VA?", a: "Deck costs in Hamilton depend on material choice. Composite deck replacement runs $25,000 to $40,000 for 300 square feet. Western red cedar runs $22,000 to $35,000 for 300 square feet. Ipe hardwood runs $30,000 to $50,000. Large custom decks (500+ square feet, feasible on Hamilton's larger lots) run $50,000 to $90,000. Older home structural remediation adds $2,000 to $7,000 when ledger or rim joist repair is needed." },
      { q: "What deck materials are popular in western Loudoun and Hamilton VA?", a: "Western Loudoun homeowners request a wider range of materials than eastern Loudoun's planned communities. Composite decking (Trex, TimberTech, AZEK) is popular for low maintenance. Western red cedar is chosen for its natural appearance and compatibility with older colonial and rural homes. Ipe hardwood is selected for premium durability and appearance on higher-specification projects. Pressure-treated wood remains an option for budget projects or utilitarian outbuildings. LDN Decks builds in all these materials." },
      { q: "What structural issues should I expect on an older Hamilton area home?", a: "Hamilton-area homes built before 1995 often have ledger connections and rim joist conditions that do not meet current Loudoun County code standards. Original PT ledgers may be face-nailed rather than through-bolted, or may lack flashing that meets current requirements. Rim joist deterioration from moisture accumulation behind an unflashed ledger is a common finding. LDN Decks evaluates ledger and rim joist condition at estimate time on all western Loudoun older-home projects and addresses remediation needs as part of the project scope." }
